I'm playing a knight when I fall through a trap door that takes me
down 2 levels, from 6 to 8.  I find the upstairs to level 7 and wind
up in the middle of a large (8x5) leprechaun hall.  Now, being a
stealthy knight, I don't want to incur alignment penalties for
attacking 40 sleeping monsters, nor do I want to wake them all up. 
Tracking down 40 leprechauns running around a level is NOT a fun way
to spend an hour or so.  This leaves out kicking the wall, playing an
instrument or knocking down some nearby doors.  Ditto playing an
instrument, or any other loud noises.

I finally jumped to one conclusion, though... As a knight, you have
inherent jumping.  Unlike chess knights, you cannot pass over an
intervening monster... rather you bump into it.  This wakes up the
first monster in your way, but does not result in a "You caitiff"
alignment hit, nor does it wake up other monsters...

I don't remember seeing this as a knightly tactic, nor if its
considered an abuse, but I thought others might like to share this
tactic.

